  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "In a bubble inheritance opened by flying sword Immortal Gu, a skeleton falls from a stone pillar space about the size of a vat. The skeleton is full of bone path dao marks and is a quasi rank eight immortal material.",
      "chapters": [
        1156
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "quasi-rank-eight-bones",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Sealed thoughts in the skull explain that the skeleton is not the inheritance’s creator but an enemy killed by the information path Gu Immortal who left the site. That Gu Immortal says the skeleton can be used as immortal material directly because the enemy’s dao marks were all left inside it. After a Gu Immortal dies, dao marks usually return to the immortal aperture; gathering them into the skeleton and preserving them is treated as an unusual information path method.",
      "chapters": [
        1156
      ],
